  "title": "Exact Worst-Case Success Probability for Increasing Event Kernels on K₅ at p = 1/2",
  "batch_label": "48",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For the frozen K_5 problem at p=1/2, let F(r), 3/4 <= r <= 1, be the minimum unconditional success probability over every admissible jointly defined family of auxiliary events with each event probability at least r. Then F(r) equals (182/207)r on [3/4,207/256], (19/18)r-73/512 on [207/256,243/256], (4/3)r-13/32 on [243/256,63/64], and 2r-17/16 on [63/64,1]. In particular, for r=1-t^2 and every 0<t<=1/2, F(1-t^2)>(15/16)(1-2t), so the frozen inequality holds for the complete p=1/2 slice.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
